Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:32:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(graph):=20sends=20on=20the=20audio=20bridg?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20=E2=80=94=20copy-mode=20tap,=20aux=20return=20as=20N=20brid?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ge=20readers=20sharing=20one=20declared=20latency?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A send is an engine-only plugin that writes a ring; the level is applied once per
block on the tap's copy (removes the automated-send defect). The aux return reads
one BridgeReader per send (registerAuxReaders), group-resolved latency, and an
aux-only container now gets a SilentNode content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
